1) All vacuums created by spells on this list also create a loud noise. The larger the radius, the louder the noise. The GM may wish to rule that all within the radius must make a second RR or be deafened for 1 round per 10 failure (RR attack level equals the radius of the vacuum).
2) An elemental creature made of gas will be cut to 20% activity if it is the target of an Air Stop spell (and the creature fits into the area of effect). A Vacuum spell thrown upon an elemental creature made of gas will result in a Slaying critical on the creature.
3) When the oxygen in an area of effect falls below 50% of normal, anyone in the area of effect must make a RR (attack level is
1) or fall asleep (this RR is modified by -2 for every 1% under 50%). Of course, if the % drops below 10%, suffocation becomes a danger. All fire spells in an area of low oxygen are modified by -2 (or -2 % effectiveness for non-attack spells) for every 1% under 50% of normal oxygen. SORCERER BASE LIST 3.7.3 GAS DESTRUCTION
